window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-6e39401d1f472a38"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"connect-computers-and-apps-to-your-dot\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dot\">将电脑和应用连接到 dot（专属智能体）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>dot 运行在云端，并拥有自己的云端电脑和浏览器。即使你自己的电脑关机，dot 仍然保持可用。连接你自己的电脑和应用后，dot 就能访问更多与你工作有关的内容。这些连接与<a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">用于联系 dot 的消息渠道</a>彼此独立。dot 在云端工作或协调已连接电脑上的工作时，你可以通过手机向它发送请求。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-cloud-computer\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">使用云端电脑</h2> <p>打开 dot 的个人资料，在 <strong>电脑（Computers）</strong> 下查看它的云端电脑。dot 提供浏览器接管选项时，你也可以选择 <strong>打开电脑（Open computer）</strong>。</p> <p>打开电脑并不代表你已经取得控制权。选择 <strong>接管（Take over）</strong>，即可使用它的鼠标和键盘；dot 可以继续工作时，再选择 <strong>交还控制权（Return control）</strong>。</p> <p>你可以使用云端电脑开展研究、处理文档、分析数据或开发软件。即使你的设备关机，云端工作仍可继续；两次使用之间，云端电脑也可以保留状态。它拥有独立的文件、软件和浏览器会话。你在自己的电脑上登录某个网站，并不会让 dot 自动登录该网站。</p> <p><a id=\"cloud-threads\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">云端线程</h2> <p>dot 可以为云端工作开启独立线程。这些线程会显示在桌面、网页和移动应用中；dot 继续协调工作时，你可以查看结果并补充指示。编程任务需要使用代码仓库和配置时，它可以使用你已设置好的 Codex 云端环境。</p> <p>dot 可以并行处理多项工作；这些线程运行期间，你也可以继续与它交谈。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"sign-in-to-a-website\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">登录网站</h2> <p>dot 使用与 ChatGPT Work 相同的私密登录流程。网站需要登录时，dot 可以通过私密表单向你发送请求。请在表单中输入凭据，并完成网站要求的验证（例如验证码）。这些信息会由表单发送给远程浏览器，不会进入对话。</p> <p>你也可以选择直接在网站上登录。这会以接管模式打开 dot 的浏览器，让你自行完成登录步骤。准备好让 dot 继续时，请交还控制权。</p> <p><a id=\"staying-signed-in\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">保持登录状态</h3> <p>网站会话可以留待后续工作使用，直到你退出登录或网站使该会话失效。dot 的云端浏览器使用独立会话，不会继承你个人浏览器中的登录状态。有些网站会屏蔽云端浏览器或要求额外验证。</p> <p><a id=\"saving-and-reusing-a-login\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">保存并重复使用登录信息</h3> <p>如果出现 <strong>保存到密码管理器（Save to Passwords）</strong> 选项，你可以保存登录信息，以供以后登录时使用。保存是可选的。发起新的登录请求时，如果有匹配的已保存登录信息，你可以确认使用它，也可以改用其他账户。</p> <p>已保存的登录信息与有效的网站会话并不是一回事。dot 可以继续使用仍有效的会话，而不必再次登录。要重新登录并使用已保存的凭据，仍须得到你的确认。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-your-computer\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">连接你的电脑</h2> <p>只需连接一次电脑，即可让 dot 在工作中使用该电脑的本地文件、代码和应用：</p> <ol> <li>在这台电脑的 ChatGPT 应用中打开 dot 的个人资料。</li> <li>在 <strong>电脑（Computers）</strong> 下找到 <strong>你的电脑（Your computer）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>允许访问（Allow access）</strong>。</li> <li>查看确认信息，再次选择 <strong>允许访问（Allow access）</strong> 以完成连接。</li> </ol> <p>每次只能连接一台个人电脑。dot 的云端电脑会保持连接。只要联系的是同一个 dot，你在任何渠道（包括手机）都可以使用这台电脑的访问能力。</p> <p>dot 可以创建本地 Work 或 Codex 任务，也可以继续处理已有的本地 Codex 任务。任务可以由云端进行管理，同时使用已连接电脑上的文件和工具。打开任务即可查看工作实际运行的位置，或直接补充指示。任务类型和连接要求请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p>如果网站屏蔽云端浏览器，可以让 dot 尝试使用已连接的电脑。这可能会创建一个独立的本地任务，但不会转移云端浏览器的会话，也不保证支持某个特定的本地浏览器。</p> <p>任务之间，电脑连接会保持有效。dot 使用电脑期间，请保持电脑联网并打开 ChatGPT 应用。 状态显示为 <strong>离线（Offline）</strong> 意味着电脑暂不可用，并不代表连接已撤销。选择 <strong>撤销访问权限（Revoke access）</strong> 才会移除访问权限。dot 的本地电脑权限，与将电脑连接到 Codex 或启用 Work Sync 相互独立；单独建立其中任一种连接，都不会自动授予 dot 访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-apps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">连接应用</h2> <p>dot 可以使用已为你的账户安装并启用的受支持<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>。访问能力取决于插件连接的账户、相应权限，以及工作实际运行的环境。本地技能需要连接电脑。</p> <p>例如，连接 Gmail 以查找相关邮件，连接 Google Drive 以读取和更新文档，或连接 GitHub 以调查问题并准备拉取请求。请安装并连接你希望 dot 使用的每个插件。</p> <p>请检查连接账户及其允许执行的操作。dot 受你在 ChatGPT 应用中已有权限的约束。例如，你可以允许它读取邮件，但不允许它发送邮件。连接过期后，请先打开请求并重新连接，再继续工作。</p> <p>添加联系方式不会授予 dot 访问应用或电脑的权限。例如，在 Slack 中给 dot 发消息，并不会连接你的收件箱。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"connect-computers-and-apps-to-your-dot\">Connect computers and apps to your dot</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Your dot lives in the cloud and has its own computer and browser. It stays available when your computer is off. Connecting your own computer and apps gives it access to more of your work. These connections are separate from the <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">channels you use to message your dot</a>. You can send a request from your phone while your dot works in the cloud or coordinates work on a connected computer.</p> <h2 id=\"use-the-cloud-computer\">Use the cloud computer</h2> <p>Open your dot's profile and look under <strong>Computers</strong> to inspect its cloud computer. You can also select <strong>Open computer</strong> when your dot offers a browser handoff.</p> <p>Opening the computer doesn't give you control. Select <strong>Take over</strong> to use its mouse and keyboard, then <strong>Return control</strong> when your dot can continue.</p> <p>Use the cloud computer for research, documents, data analysis, or software work. Cloud work can continue while your devices are off, and the computer can keep its state between periods of use. It has its own files, software, and browser sessions. Signing in to a website on your computer doesn't sign your dot in to that website.</p> <h2 id=\"cloud-threads\">Cloud threads</h2> <p>Your dot can start separate threads for cloud work. These appear in your desktop, web, and mobile apps, where you can review results and give further instructions while your dot continues coordinating. For coding work, it can use a Codex cloud environment you’ve set up with the repository and configuration it needs.</p> <p>Your dot can work on several things in parallel, and you can keep talking to it while those threads run. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">Tasks and memory</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"sign-in-to-a-website\">Sign in to a website</h2> <p>Your dot uses the same private sign-in flow as ChatGPT Work. When a website needs a login, your dot can send a request with a private form. Enter your credentials there and complete any verification the website requires, such as a verification code. The form sends this information to the remote browser outside your conversation.</p> <p>You can also choose to sign in on the website instead. This opens your dot's browser in takeover mode so you can complete the steps yourself. Return control when you're ready for your dot to continue.</p> <h3 id=\"staying-signed-in\">Staying signed in</h3> <p>A website session can remain available for later work until you sign out or the website expires it. Your dot's cloud browser has its own sessions; it doesn't inherit logins from your personal browser. Some websites block cloud browsers or require further verification.</p> <h3 id=\"saving-and-reusing-a-login\">Saving and reusing a login</h3> <p>When offered, <strong>Save to Passwords</strong> lets you save a login for future sign-ins. Saving is optional. If a matching saved login is available for a new sign-in request, you can confirm that you want to use it or enter another account.</p> <p>A saved login and an active website session are different. Your dot can continue using a valid session without signing in again. Reusing a saved login to sign in requires your confirmation.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-your-computer\">Connect your computer</h2> <p>Connect your computer once to make its local files, code, and apps available for your dot’s work:</p> <ol> <li>Open your dot's profile in the ChatGPT app on that computer.</li> <li>Under <strong>Computers</strong>, find <strong>Your computer</strong> and select <strong>Allow access</strong>.</li> <li>Review the confirmation and select <strong>Allow access</strong> to connect it.</li> </ol> <p>You can connect only one personal computer at a time. Your dot’s cloud computer stays connected. Access to your computer applies wherever you message the same dot, including from your phone.</p> <p>Your dot can create local Work or Codex tasks and continue existing local Codex tasks. A task can be managed in the cloud while using files and tools on your connected computer. Open the task to inspect where the work is happening or give instructions directly. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">Tasks and memory</a> for task types and connection requirements.</p> <p>If a website blocks the cloud browser, ask your dot to try your connected computer. This may create a separate local task. It doesn't transfer the cloud browser's session or guarantee that a particular local browser is supported.</p> <p>The connection persists between tasks. Keep your computer online and the ChatGPT app open while your dot uses it. An <strong>Offline</strong> status means the computer is unavailable; it doesn't revoke the connection. Select <strong>Revoke access</strong> to remove access. Your dot's local-computer permission is separate from connecting a computer to Codex or enabling Work Sync. Neither connection alone gives your dot access.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-apps\">Connect apps</h2> <p>Your dot can use supported <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> installed and enabled for your account. Access depends on the plugin’s connected account, permissions, and the environment where the work runs. Local skills require a connected computer.</p> <p>For example, connect Gmail to find relevant email, Google Drive to read and update documents, or GitHub to investigate an issue and prepare a pull request. Install and connect each plugin you want your dot to use.</p> <p>Review the connected account and its allowed actions. Your existing ChatGPT app permissions apply to your dot. For example, you can allow it to read email without allowing it to send email. If a connection expires, open the request to reconnect it before continuing.</p> <p>Adding a contact method doesn't grant access to your apps or computer. For example, messaging your dot in Slack doesn't connect your inbox.</p>"};
